    "body": "## Motivation\n\nAfter loading new weights, every `update_weights_*` path flushes the cache and asserts that the flush succeeded. The flush is refused while requests are running or queued, which is the normal state after `pause_generation(mode=\"in_place\")`, or after a retract pause that left requests behind. The assert then kills the scheduler, and with it the whole server.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- `SchedulerWeightUpdaterManager.flush_cache_after_weight_update` returns a failed result with a message when the flush is refused, instead of asserting. The disk, distributed, tensor and IPC paths pass it through as `success=False`.\n- The new weights stay loaded and their version is recorded, as before; only the result changes from a crash to a failed call that says to retract or finish the requests and call `/flush_cache`.\n\n## Checks\n\n- Qwen3-0.6B, one request running, `pause_generation(mode=\"in_place\")`, then `update_weights_from_disk`:\n  - main: the scheduler exits on `Cache flush failed after updating weights` and the server is gone.\n  - This PR: the update returns 400 with the message; `continue_generation` and `/health` succeed.\n- Unit tests under `test/registered/unit/managers/scheduler_components/` and `managers/`: same results as main.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:no_entry_sign: [Run #38204785729](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38204785729)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #38204785576](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38204785576)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:no_entry_sign: [Run #38204785968](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38204785968)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->\n",
